00:02:27.420 --> 00:02:29.070
Around 80 years ago,

00:02:29.070 --> 00:02:33.300
Ashihara investigated the massive 
red tide that occurred in this area,

00:02:33.300 --> 00:02:35.390
and it was then that he found this special jellyfish.

00:02:35.390 --> 00:02:38.010
It seems he conducted his research at this facility.

00:02:38.010 --> 00:02:40.890
Jellyfish? Not observing radio waves, huh?

00:02:42.520 --> 00:02:45.370
He'd be over 100 years old if he was still alive.

00:02:45.940 --> 00:02:48.150
We don't really know if he's dead.

00:02:48.900 --> 00:02:52.530
Do jellyfish emit radio waves?

00:02:53.030 --> 00:02:54.490
Saranga?

00:02:54.490 --> 00:02:57.370
It's what the staff named the monster.

00:02:57.370 --> 00:03:02.040
Ashihara also predicted the appearance 
of the creatures based on the red dust.

00:03:02.040 --> 00:03:03.410
What is its goal?

00:03:04.080 --> 00:03:07.880
Perhaps it's aiming for some fresh air on the surface.

00:03:07.880 --> 00:03:09.710
If Ashihara is correct,

00:03:09.710 --> 00:03:13.510
we should also consider that 
it's after the treasure we stole.

00:03:14.630 --> 00:03:16.130
Could it be... SHIVA?

00:03:16.130 --> 00:03:18.720
It destroyed the wall in just one day.

00:03:18.720 --> 00:03:20.930
The rest won't hold for much longer.

00:03:20.930 --> 00:03:22.140
How much time do we have?

00:03:22.140 --> 00:03:27.650
A more important matter is that
 phase alpha of the red dust has been stabilized.

00:03:28.190 --> 00:03:35.400
It took ten years being stuck in a lab 
to materialize it for just one millisecond.

00:03:35.400 --> 00:03:40.160
Along with the appearance of Rodan, the damage 
caused by red dust is spreading across various areas.

00:03:40.160 --> 00:03:46.250
As airlines are unable to ensure protection of their engines 
against the red dust, flights have been suspended,

00:03:46.250 --> 00:03:49.000
and the piling up of red dust is causing electrical—

00:03:49.500 --> 00:03:52.390
Annals of Artificial Chemistry...

00:03:52.780 --> 00:03:56.270
1960, Volume 18.

00:03:56.890 --> 00:03:58.220
Where's the next volume?

00:03:58.220 --> 00:04:01.680
It's on the shelf 10 meters ahead and 2 meters to your left.

00:04:01.680 --> 00:04:05.680
Sigh... It's just packed full of niche magazines.

00:04:06.270 --> 00:04:08.310
How are you holding up in that new body?

00:04:08.310 --> 00:04:12.360
Its specs are 256 times better than your PC!

00:04:12.360 --> 00:04:16.320
Didn't you say your personality 
was closely tied to that PC?

00:04:16.320 --> 00:04:19.180
Come now, let's not sweat the details.

00:04:19.570 --> 00:04:21.410
It's not here.

00:04:21.410 --> 00:04:24.660
Ashihara was Archetype's initial researcher,

00:04:24.660 --> 00:04:28.290
but no one could understand most of his research.

00:04:29.040 --> 00:04:31.210
He really was a heretic.

00:04:31.210 --> 00:04:34.130
His work is only in magazines 
that don't seem to have been digitized.

00:04:34.130 --> 00:04:39.720
The fact that his research isn't published in famous magazines means either he got rejected or he refused those offers.

00:04:39.720 --> 00:04:42.350
What if it was simply wrong?

00:04:42.350 --> 00:04:43.600
Maybe.

00:04:44.140 --> 00:04:45.350
This is it!

00:04:49.600 --> 00:04:52.270
So this is Professor Ashihara...

00:04:54.610 --> 00:04:55.980
A fish?

00:04:55.980 --> 00:04:57.070
And a dog?

00:04:57.610 --> 00:04:59.860
It looks like a diagram of sporadic simple groups.

00:04:59.860 --> 00:05:03.240
Well, it's no wonder it wasn't 
published in any proper magazines.

00:05:03.240 --> 00:05:07.350
I have no idea what any of this is about. 
Looks like scribbles.

00:05:08.350 --> 00:05:13.720
"Let's your soul stand cool and 
composed before a million universes."

00:05:15.130 --> 00:05:17.000
Fearful symmetry?

00:05:17.000 --> 00:05:19.920
It looks very similar to your notes.

00:05:19.920 --> 00:05:22.130
Orthogonal diagonalizer?

00:05:25.600 --> 00:05:27.620
6=9?

00:05:28.230 --> 00:05:29.640
What does it mean?

